<title>UK: Stasco official, former minister join IPE board.</title>
<headline>Stasco official, former minister join IPE board.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The International Petroleum Exchange (IPE) said on Wednesday it had appointed Shell International Trading and Shipping (Stasco) executive Peter Ward and former U.K. trade minister Lord Fraser to its board.</p>
<p>Ward, a Stasco vice-president for crude trading, joins the board immediately.</p>
<p>Fraser, former minister of state at the Department of Trade and Industry with responsibility for energy, will become one of the exchange's two lay directors and will take up his appointment in September.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 7646</p>
